TYPES.md §7.2, DECISIONS 460: a Duration negation is computed without wrapping, so `-(-9223372036854775808ms)` is E3201 on its true value, 2^63 ms, never on the wrapped -2^63 ms, with or without an expected type; `-(-(9223372036854ms))` fits. The value is what is stored, so a typed declaration names it (API.md §4.4 F12). A token of 2^63 ms not folded into a `-` is E1111 alone (TestLexErrorInLiteralRange).
